{"styles":[{"sc":"#ff2600","so":1,"w":2,"ol":true,"fc":"#fffb00","fo":0.502}],"cards":["<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#222222;max-width:238px;\"><div style=\"background:#0e7d46;height:6px;border-radius:3px 3px 0 0;\"></div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:7px 0 0;\">COUNTY BOUNDARY</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:0 0 2px;\">GEORGIA</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-weight:800;padding:2px 0 6px;\">Clayton County</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;\"><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Population</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">297,703 (2024 est.)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">County Seat</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">Jonesboro</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Land Area</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">142 sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Density</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">2,096 / sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Household Income</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$60,067</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Home Value</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$264,900</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#333333;padding:8px 0 2px;border-top:1px solid #eef2f1;margin-top:7px;\">Clayton County sits immediately south of Atlanta and is defined economically by Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta International Airport, whose footprint and workforce — including Delta Air Lines' Technical Operations base — anchor a logistics-driven economy where supply chain, warehousing, and air cargo account for a large share of local jobs. Forest Park and the Clayton-side edge of College Park have built out extensive industrial and distribution space feeding off airport access and the convergence of I-75, I-285, and I-675. Jonesboro, the county seat, retains a historic small-town core, while Riverdale, Morrow, and Lake City offer more conventional suburban retail and residential product. Incomes and home values trail the metro Atlanta average, making the county a value-oriented market for both industrial and workforce housing investment, with e-commerce and air-cargo growth continuing to drive demand for logistics space near the airport.</div><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888888;padding-top:6px;\">Source: U.S. Census Bureau · Data verified: August 22, 2026</div></div>"],"feats":[["Clayton",0,[[33.38992,-84.3934],[33.39008,-84.39336],[33.39084,-84.39293],[33.39111,-84.39297],[33.39126,-84.39343],[33.39116,-84.39392],[33.39091,-84.39415],[33.39107,-84.39442],[33.39134,-84.39428],[33.392,-84.39403],[33.39293,-84.39437],[33.39386,-84.39303],[33.39461,-84.3928],[33.39498,-84.3922],[33.39515,-84.39102],[33.39556,-84.39097],[33.39605,-84.38976],[33.39585,-84.3891],[33.39595,-84.38871],[33.39727,-84.38825],[33.39776,-84.38755],[33.39807,-84.38735],[33.40083,-84.38719],[33.40131,-84.38635],[33.40145,-84.38436],[33.40188,-84.38419],[33.40292,-84.38431],[33.40254,-84.38467],[33.40248,-84.38497],[33.40303,-84.38558],[33.40375,-84.38593],[33.40407,-84.38681],[33.40445,-84.38717],[33.4055,-84.38747],[33.40566,-84.38742],[33.40574,-84.387],[33.40596,-84.38692],[33.40634,-84.38751],[33.40697,-84.38757],[33.40978,-84.38675],[33.41167,-84.38831],[33.41184,-84.39303],[33.41219,-84.3931],[33.41668,-84.39309],[33.41784,-84.39324],[33.41801,-84.39324],[33.41838,-84.39311],[33.4201,-84.39309],[33.42014,-84.39522],[33.42015,-84.39767],[33.42034,-84.40238],[33.4217,-84.40238],[33.42171,-84.40234],[33.4219,-84.40238